parents I know you find yourselves at  home with who knows what kind of  textbooks and what kind of advice from  your teacher and I thought I'd give you  four basic tips that you can use to be  successful with homeschooling number one  this is a very important time for  parents and teachers to work together  you have always been partnered with the  teacher of your child but good  communication between parent and teacher  has never been more important so feel  free to email teachers make sure that  you understand what they're saying and  give them feedback about what you're  seeing at home remember teachers have  never been through this either and they  need information from you in order to do  it successfully number two this is a  great opportunity to remember that  education is not about jumping through  hoops the schedule of the school day is  usually a pretty rigorous schedule  students are in school from around eight  o'clock to around three o'clock and  they've got all kinds of activities  aren't music PE the kinds of things that  it just doesn't make sense to replicate  when you're at home so parents give  yourselves a little bit of grace  remember that it may not be possible to  do every single activity that your kids  are used to doing during the school day  and that's okay this is an opportunity  for us to think about what we really  want out of our children's education and  to focus on the true essence the really  important things that we want our kids  to learn number three keep things simple  it's very easy I think to spend a lot of  our time right now thinking about the  technicalities thinking about what is  the perfect system that will enable us  to keep things moving and we don't need  to worry about that right now  there are a bunch of things that our  students already know how to do that are  really worth doing so for example  reading great literature this is a time  to pick up that book that you loved when  you were a child or to pick up a book  that you've always wanted to read with  your child and spend some time as a  family spend some time reading that book  to those children number four  encourage organization and structure get  some habits in place now that will serve  you well next week next month maybe even  two or three months down the road we  don't know how long this is going to  last but we know that if we put some  structure behind our  work that it will make things more  smooth down the road above all whether  you're a teacher or a parent now is the  time to think about quality over  quantity don't focus on the amount of  work the number of objectives a child  was going to achieve for this trimester  or quarter instead think about the  quality of the work that the children  are doing and let that be your guide  you
 

